  "body": "Found by the QA swarm round 2 (#2582), brief q05 (4th-axis block), CamCraft **v0.25.0** Linux x86_64 release; the order reproduced by hand.\n\n## What happens\n\n```\nadd_setup {\"name\": \"Setup1\"}                              -> \"setups\": [\"Setup1\"]\nadd_setup {\"name\": \"Front_A90\", \"datum_from\": \"Setup1\"}   -> \"setups\": [\"Front_A90\", \"Setup1\"]\n```\n\n`get_job` lists the setups in the same name order, and the post follows it: the agent's [test-probe.nc](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q05-4axis/test-probe.nc) runs `(SETUP: Front_A90)` (line 4) before `(SETUP: Setup1)` (line 38), with the setup-change stop between them, although Front_A90 was created after Setup1 and takes its datum (and its carried stock) from it. Renaming it `Setup2_A90` put it second. There is no MCP tool to reorder setups.\n\nThis is the setup-level twin of #3022 (operations re-sorted by name, fixed in v0.25.0).\n\n## Expected\n\nSetups keep the order they were created in (or an order the user sets), and the post runs them in that order. A setup whose stock is carried from another never posts before it.\n\n## Repro files\n\n[q05-4axis.step](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q05-4axis/q05-4axis.step), [probe.camproj](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q05-4axis/probe.camproj), [test-probe.nc](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q05-4axis/test-probe.nc); agent report [REPORT.md](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q05-4axis/REPORT.md) problem 7.\n\nDone means: two setups added as Setup1 then Front_A90 stay in that order in add_setup, get_job and the posted program (pinned by a test), and a reorder command (with its MCP tool) exists or is filed.\n",
